{
  "studio.about": "About Mapping studio",
  "studio.about.canvas": "Drag the canvas to pan. Lay Out Mapping arranges the expression from left to right at its fixed scale. Copying a function also copies its input branches. Paste adds a separate copy, with no connection to the target. Delete Floating Objects removes all objects and branches that have no path to the target. A check mark means complete, an exclamation mark indicates a missing input or an incomplete dependency, and a dash means there is no path to the target.",
  "studio.about.connect": "Drag a source field onto a target for a direct connection. In its expression, drag from an output to an input to connect them. Dropping on an occupied input replaces its wire. Move either end of a wire to reconnect it, or right-click it and choose Disconnect. To connect with the keyboard, focus a node, press Shift+F10 and choose Connect to.",
  "studio.about.open": "Open a mapping from its Rail8 package. Choose Edit to make changes.",
  "studio.about.parameters": "Double-click a function with parameters or use its gear to edit them. Right-click a node and choose Display Queue to show its queue in the last test run. Save writes the mapping file to the workspace. Test runs the mapping on the service.",
